WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.277
Let's talk about the role of organisations
in promoting mental health.

2
00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:06.947
Organisations play a strategic role

3
00:00:07.030 --> 00:00:09.817
in promoting their employees'
mental health.

4
00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:13.827
Not only because work takes up
a significant part of people's lives,

5
00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:18.057
but also because it is in this context
that many of their relationships,

6
00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:20.677
routines and demands take shape.

7
00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:22.267
It is often in the workplace

8
00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:26.607
that the first signs
of psychological distress appear,

9
00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:29.657
such as changes in behaviour,
extreme tiredness, irritability,

10
00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:32.617
difficulty concentrating or isolation.

11
00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:35.527
When organisations
are attentive and prepared,

12
00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:38.477
these signs can be recognised
in good time,

13
00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:41.589
allowing a more appropriate response.

14
00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:43.997
Beyond identifying distress,

15
00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:47.797
the greatest potential
of organisations lies in prevention.

16
00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:51.707
Promoting healthy environments
means developing an organisational

17
00:00:51.790 --> 00:00:54.837
culture centred on respect, listening,

18
00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:57.208
fairness and valuing people.

19
00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:03.737
When these conditions are present,
relationships become more cooperative,

20
00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:04.797
motivation increases,

21
00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:10.538
productivity improves and the risk
of burnout and absenteeism falls.

22
00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:14.107
At the same time,
factors such as work-life balance,

23
00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:19.057
job security, trust in leadership
and access to psychological support

24
00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:22.112
are key elements in promoting well-being.

25
00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:27.577
Promoting mental health at work
is not an optional extra,

26
00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:31.417
but an essential dimension
of how organisations function.

27
00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:34.467
All organisations,
whatever their size or sector,

28
00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:37.325
have an active role in this process.
